---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How to Play 16-0play | Cricket Strategy Guide"
  description="Learn how to draft your team, manage player form, and achieve a perfect 16-0 season in our definitive guide to 16-0play."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-20 text-[var(--color-body)] text-base leading-relaxed">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-[var(--color-ink)] tracking-tight mb-8">How to Play 16-0play</h1>
    
    <p class="text-lg mb-10">
      16-0play is a strategic cricket simulator where your goal is to assemble the ultimate playing XI and guide them to a perfect, undefeated 16-match season. Below is everything you need to know to get started.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-12">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-4">1. Drafting Your Team</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The foundation of a successful season is a well-balanced squad. You have access to a massive database of cricket legends and modern stars. 
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li><strong>Batters (BAT):</strong> You need a solid top and middle order to set or chase high scores.</li>
          <li><strong>Bowlers (BOWL):</strong> A diverse bowling attack prevents opponents from scoring freely.</li>
          <li><strong>All-Rounders (AR):</strong> The glue of any team. They provide vital balance and flexibility.</li>
          <li><strong>Wicketkeepers (WK):</strong> Essential for both batting depth and fielding chemistry.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A team stacked entirely with batters will lose matches due to a weak bowling attack. Balance is key.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-4">2. The Match Engine</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Once your team is locked in, you will face a schedule of 16 increasingly difficult opponents. Matches are simulated instantly using a comprehensive algorithm that calculates win probability based on:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li>The combined rating of your starting XI.</li>
          <li>The balance of roles (penalties apply if you lack enough bowlers or batters).</li>
          <li>Dynamic match conditions and randomized variance to simulate the unpredictability of T20 cricket.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-4">3. Managing Form</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Players don't just rely on their base rating. Throughout the season, player form fluctuates based on match outcomes and individual simulation events.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pay attention to the <strong>Form Sparkline</strong> in the player UI. A player on a hot streak will over-perform their base rating, while a player in a slump might need to be carefully managed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-4">4. Achieving the 16-0 Dream</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          One single loss ends your perfect run. However, you can choose to complete the season to register a 14-2 or 15-1 record on the global leaderboard. 
        </p>
        <p>
          To achieve 16-0, you will need a perfectly constructed team, excellent form management, and a little bit of luck when facing elite opponents in the final matches. Good luck!
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
